exit: 0
--- stdout
CPU level x86_64 (x86_64-pc-linux-gnu), widest vector register 16 bytes

add_arrays (line 6)
  vector types:
    f32x8: 2 × xmm (split)
  split or emulated:
    line 8: f32x8 + is split: one instruction per register
  masked tails:
    line 7: the last block is one masked step (a short sequence of loads, blends and stores)

divide (line 12)
  vector types:
    i32x16: 4 × xmm (split)
  split or emulated:
    line 13: i32x16 / is emulated: one lane at a time (no vector integer division)

times (line 16)
  vector types:
    u64x4: 2 × xmm (split)
  split or emulated:
    line 17: u64x4 * is emulated: three multiplies per lane pair (vpmullq needs AVX-512)

total (line 20)
  vector types:
    f32x4: 1 × xmm
  masked tails:
    line 24: the last block is one masked step (a short sequence of loads, blends and stores)
  multiversion copies:
    x86_64_v3 (vector registers of 32 bytes)
    x86_64_v4 (vector registers of 64 bytes)
    x86_64 (the build's own level, for CPUs below those)

scale (line 30)
  must_vectorize loops:
    line 32: vectorized
